  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referencing the **Georgia Department of Revenue's Motor Vehicle Division (MVD)** tag renewal portal. Here's a summary of what that page is for:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\ude97 Georgia MVD \u2013 Tag Renewal Portal\n**URL:** [https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx](https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx)\n\nGeorgia MVD offers online applications and information regarding **tag renewals, license plates, titles, dealer registrations, and commercial vehicles**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd04 What You Can Do on This Page:\n- **Renew your vehicle registration (tag) online** \u2014 This is the primary function of the page.\n- Georgia residents can renew their registration online at this portal. However, **if the address on your Renewal Notice is not correct, do not renew online.**\n- You must **present your driver's license or Georgia ID** to renew.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb Additional Services Available Through Georgia MVD:\n- Request services **without re-entering VINs, license plates, or driver's license numbers** each time, quickly access vehicles associated with your driver's license, and request a replacement title online.\n- After vehicle registration, you will receive a **license plate with a decal which must be renewed each year**. Georgia also offers information on ordering **specialty and prestige (vanity) license plates**, with hundreds of specialty plate designs to choose from, including veterans, colleges, and special interest groups.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Important Notes:\n- An owner has **seven (7) calendar days** from the purchase or transfer date, or the date they establish residency in Georgia, to title and register their vehicle. If you fail to register during this period, you will be subject to fines if stopped by law enforcement.\n- Georgia requires a **Title Ad Valorem Tax of 6.6%** (beginning 01/01/2020) to be paid at the time of titling.\n- Local, state, and federal government websites often end in .gov. State of Georgia government websites and email systems use \"georgia.gov\" or \"ga.gov\" at the end of the address. **Before sharing sensitive or personal information, make sure you're on an official state website.**\n\n---\n\nWould you need help with anything specific, such as renewing a tag, finding a tag office, or understanding fees?",
